A1. This swims around Newfoundland. ~ COD
A4. This is all wrong. ~ MISTAKE
A10. This kind of runner didn't go to the Olympic games. ~ RUM
A13. So be it! ~ AMEN
A15. About the first thing a doughboy met in France. ~ LOUSE
A16. This gives a porcupine a stuck-up appearance. ~ SETA
A17. This is just a comment. ~ REMARK
A19. When the roll is called there will be many missing—where? ~ YONDER
A21. A hub. ~ NAVE
A22. This is high up in the fashion world. ~ HEN
A24. These are always getting up in arms about something. ~ FOES
A26. An Eastern state. (Abbr.) ~ NY
A27. Manner. ~ MODUS
A29. Through the agency of. ~ BY
A31. This helps keep the younger generation on the straight and narrow. ~ ROD
A33. No matter how you slice it, it's this just the same. ~ BOLOGNA
A35. This fish is all neck. ~ EEL
A37. A preposition. ~ ON
A38. To give up or surrender. ~ CEDE
A39. Magnitude or bulk. ~ SIZE
A41. The woman who pays. ~ MA
A42. A Heffin broadside. ~ TIRADE
A43. This lays around a lot. ~ PULLET
A44. A cry or call to excite attention. ~ HO
A45. This should be saved for a rainy day. ~ PELF
A47. This carries disease. ~ GERM
A48. This means "nothing doing." ~ NO
A49. We wouldn't meet this if we lived forever. ~ END
A51. These kind of workers are always digging into the underworld. ~ WELFARE
A53. Bustle. ~ ADO
A54. A part of the verb "to be." ~ IS
A56. These hold a lot of relics of by-gone days. ~ RUINS
A57. Any, each, or one. ~ AN
A58. A lot of people are swindled by this. ~ FAKE
A60. This often gets a beating. ~ EGG
A61. Part of the foot. ~ INCH
A63. The kind of climbers they have in Switzerland. ~ ALPINE
A65. A composition set to sacred music. ~ ANTHEM
A67. What snoopers do who look into things. ~ PEEP
A68. A Himalayan antelope. ~ GORAL
A71. This is sure to hurt your feelings. ~ SORE
A72. This carries the corn. ~ EAR
A73. Big bosses. ~ FOREMEN
A74. You must have pull to do this. ~ ROW

D1. A rattler. ~ CAR
D2. If you believe in signs you'll get this. ~ OMEN
D3. This claim is urgent. ~ DEMAND
D5. Of the likes of. ~ ILK
D6. Therefore. ~ SO
D7. This should suit you for dinner. ~ TUXEDO
D8. Comparable or proportionate to. ~ AS
D9. This usually lets you in on the ground floor. ~ KEY
D10. The spirit of the West. ~ REDEYE
D11. A gang of scalpers. ~ UTES
D12. To disfigure. ~ MAR
D14. This is usually at sea. ~ NAVY
D16. A would-be aristocrat. ~ SNOB
D18. In law, of the thing or matter. ~ RE
D20. A preposition. ~ OF
D22. What golfers aim at. ~ HOLE
D23. These hold a lot of beer—in Germany. ~ NUGS
D25. Your father's son. ~ BROTHER
D27. One who makes a small imitation of the real thing. ~ MODELER
D28. These shoot from under cover. ~ SNIPERS
D30. Part of a military unit. ~ PLATOON
D32. A lot of people shed tears over this. ~ ONION
D33. To moisten gently. ~ BEDEW
D34. This is blue. ~ AZURE
D36. To remove errors from. ~ EMEND
D38. A lid. ~ CAP
D40. A shady thing. ~ ELM
D46. This is where things go up in smoke. ~ FLUE
D47. A Chicago fighting unit. ~ GANG
D50. A garment worn in the early ages. ~ DIAPER
D52. This is full of dangerous curves. ~ FIGURE
D53. This keeps a ship in touch with land. ~ ANCHOR
D55. To gambol. ~ SKIP
D57. These are always digging in. ~ ANTS
D58. This insect has bouncing babies. ~ FLEA
D59. A printer's measure. ~ EN
D61. At home. ~ IN
D62. A leading man at the opera. ~ HERO
D63. An ancestor. ~ APE
D64. This gives a person I trouble. ~ EGO
D65. A brand of suds. ~ ALE
D66. A reminder to feed the kitty. ~ MEW
D69. This conjunction introduces an alternative. ~ OR
D70. This comes before noon. ~ AM


